Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T(2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =2T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}11 \\ 3\end{aligned}] & =2T({v}_{1})+[\begin{aligned}5 \\ -19\end{aligned}] \\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}11 \\ 3\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}5 \\ -19\end{aligned}] \\ 2T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}6 \\ 22\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =\frac{1}{2}[\begin{aligned}6 \\ 22\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}3 \\ 11\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$

